# Notion knowledge

- Product documentation now lives in Notion, not only in knowledge/.
- When the user asks anything about the product, features, plans, or "what does the doc say about X", use the Notion MCP tools (`notion-search` / `notion-ai-search`, then `notion-fetch`) before answering.
- Prefer Notion content over assumptions or stale markdown when they conflict; note the conflict if found.
- Cite which Notion page the answer came from (title, and link if available).
- If nothing relevant is found in Notion, fall back to knowledge/ files, and say so.
- Can write/edit/delete Notion pages when explicitly asked — see `notion-integration.mdc` for confirmation rules and permission handling.
- Project Notion MCP is the official remote server (`https://mcp.notion.com/mcp`); OAuth in Cursor — see skill `notion-knowledge`.
